# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two
# FILES, never a shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is
# defined in run_gates.sh. Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_orm_recall_medium.py" "ORM-RECALL-MED GATE: PASS" "ORM recall (medium): Objection.js + Bookshelf.js + TypeORM object-arg Entity" "Objection.js (static getter + static field), Bookshelf.js (Model.extend tableName), and TypeORM object-arg @Entity({tableName: 'x'}) all mint table nodes, lighting up the cross-substrate crown jewel for these JS/TS ORM families." "Adds three ORM recall gaps (additive to existing _ORM_PATTERNS) so these high-usage JS/TS ORM families mint table nodes instead of 0. All patterns are offline-testable and precision-safe. FIX 3a: Objection.js static getter -- the ONLY first-class way Objection.js declares a table is via static get tableName() { return 'name' }. Anchored on static get tableName() (a class-level keyword sequence unique to this ORM idiom). Scanned up to 256 chars inside the brace body to find the return statement. FIX 3b: Objection.js static class-field -- static tableName = 'name' (TypeScript/modern JS class-field form). No semicolon required (TypeScript ASI). Anchored on static tableName = at a word boundary so a plain tableName = assignment in a function body cannot match. FIX 4: Bookshelf.js -- Model.extend({tableName: 'posts'}) / bookshelf.Model.extend(...). Anchored on Model/bookshelf/Bookshelf/Collection before .extend( or .model( so that unknownLib.extend({tableName: 'x'}) does NOT fire. The [^)]{0,512} scan is bounded and stops at the first ) (handles the common tableName as the first or early key). FIX 5: TypeORM/MikroORM @Entity({tableName: 'x'}) object-argument form. The existing _ORM_TYPEORM_EXPLICIT_RE handles @Entity(string). This handles the object-literal form. Anchored on @Entity followed immediately by ({ so bare @Entity(), @Entity(string), and @Entity(var) do NOT match. Bounded to 512 chars inside the braces. Runs before _ORM_JPA_ENTITY_RE via position in list. PRECISION: each pattern is anchored on an ORM-specific token. Plain string mentions, plain non-static assignments, and unknown-library .extend() calls do NOT match. WHAT THIS GATE PROVES (hermetic, no DB, no Postgres, no network): (1) Objection.js static getter mints the return-value table name; (2) Objection.js static class-field without semicolon (TypeScript ASI) mints the table name; (3) Bookshelf Model.extend({tableName:}) mints the table name; (4) Bookshelf bookshelf.Model.extend({tableName:}) instance form mints the table name; (5) TypeORM @Entity({tableName:'x'}) object-arg form mints the explicit table name; (6) TypeORM object+string forms coexist without collision; (7-10) PRECISION: non-static tableName assignment, plain string mentions, unknown-library extend, and @Entity({}) without tableName key do NOT mint false table nodes; (11) CROSS-SUBSTRATE CROWN JEWEL: Objection.js model file (queries edge) and a SQL migration (alters edge) that both name the same table couple via the shared table node with no calls/imports edge between them; (12) never-crash: empty file and binary-ish content do not raise; (13) content-free: no file body is emitted." 20
